<title>USA: Uni-Marts to buy back 250,000 shrs.</title>
<headline>Uni-Marts to buy back 250,000 shrs.</headline>
<dateline>STATE COLLEGE, Pa. 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Uni-Marts Inc said Friday it plans to purchase up to 250,000 shares of its common stock, which it said it believes is undervalued.</p>
<p>The buyback will take place from time to time in the open market using general company funds, the company said.</p>
<p>Friday morning, the company's stock was trading at 6-1/2. In the past 52 weeks, it reached a high of 9-5/8, and a low of 6-1/4.</p>
<p>Uni-Marts, which operates 405 convenience stores along the East Coast, currently has about 6.7 million shares outstanding.</p>
